WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:04.980
The end of the road has only just begun, and&nbsp;
"Fast X" leaves behind plenty of questions for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:08.820
the next installment of the franchise to answer.&nbsp;
Here's what happened in all the furious action.

00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:11.447
Warning: Spoilers for "Fast X" ahead!

00:00:11.460 --> 00:00:15.900
Dominic Toretto has faced a lot of trouble in&nbsp;
his life, from international supercriminals to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:19.980
members of his own family, but he's never faced&nbsp;
anyone quite like Jason Momoa's Dante Reyes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:23.580
a psychotic mastermind with a major&nbsp;
grudge against the Toretto crew.

00:00:23.580 --> 00:00:25.680
"I'm Dante. Enchante."

00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:29.400
Dom and his friends killed Reyes' father&nbsp;
and stole the family's money stash back&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:33.000
in "Fast Five," so Dante views Dom as&nbsp;
the source of all of his suffering. He&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:35.100
makes it his mission to make Dom suffer in kind.

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:40.140
Dante sets to work dismantling the entire Toretto&nbsp;
family, and he more-or-less succeeds by the end&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:44.400
of the film, leaving almost everyone in some&nbsp;
kind of dangerous limbo. Dom himself narrowly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:49.380
escapes Dante's wrath atop a dam in Portugal. He&nbsp;
finds himself in the water below with no means of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.380 --> 00:00:53.460
escape as Dante prepares to explode the whole dam&nbsp;
and bring it down around Dom and his son Brian.

00:00:53.460 --> 00:00:57.360
Moments before, Dom remarks that Dante's&nbsp;
one mistake was leaving him with a car,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.360 --> 00:01:00.420
but now he doesn't even have that.&nbsp;
It's hard to imagine how he finds&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.420 --> 00:01:03.523
his way out of this one. We'll have to&nbsp;
wait until the next film to find out.

00:01:03.540 --> 00:01:07.980
John Cena's Jakob Toretto was only recently&nbsp;
welcomed back into the family fold after&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.980 --> 00:01:12.240
years of estrangement and resentment. After&nbsp;
redeeming himself at the end of "F9," Jakob&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.240 --> 00:01:15.900
devotes his time and considerable talent&nbsp;
to protecting Little Brian at all costs,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.900 --> 00:01:19.140
taking him to a secret hideout and then&nbsp;
trying to help him escape with Dom.

00:01:19.860 --> 00:01:20.460
"'Sup?"&nbsp;

00:01:20.460 --> 00:01:22.905
"Uncle Jakob?"
"Your dad sent me."

00:01:22.905 --> 00:01:26.160
It's clear throughout that Jakob is&nbsp;
also still carrying a lot of guilt over&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.160 --> 00:01:29.820
his previous actions. He wants to be a good&nbsp;
uncle and a good brother to prove that he's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.820 --> 00:01:33.780
earned where he is now. That desire, and the&nbsp;
guilt behind it, culminates late in the film,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.780 --> 00:01:37.620
when Jakob realizes that he's lost Brian&nbsp;
to Dante and only has one move left:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.620 --> 00:01:43.200
Sacrificing himself so Dom can get to his son.&nbsp;
Despite Dom's protests, he goes down in a blaze&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:46.920
of glory, taking out Dante's men and clearing&nbsp;
a path for his big brother to keep fighting.

00:01:46.920 --> 00:01:50.760
The film is moving really fast at this&nbsp;
point, so there's little time to mourn Jakob,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.760 --> 00:01:54.420
or to even confirm that he's actually&nbsp;
dead. It seems like he's probably gone,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.420 --> 00:01:57.044
but the fallout of his sacrifice&nbsp;
is very much yet to come.

00:01:57.060 --> 00:02:02.340
Michelle Rodriguez's Letty Ortiz is sort of the&nbsp;
odd woman out of the Toretto crew after the job in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.340 --> 00:02:06.960
Rome goes very wrong. It makes her the last major&nbsp;
fighting chance the family has against Dante.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:11.460
Letty gets picked up by the Agency very early&nbsp;
on, and she's taken to a black site where she's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.460 --> 00:02:15.540
forced to share a cell with Charlize Theron's&nbsp;
Cipher, who's already had a run-in with Dante.

00:02:15.540 --> 00:02:19.620
The two women don't get along, to say the least,&nbsp;
but Letty realizes Cipher has a way out of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.620 --> 00:02:23.760
black site. When she gets word from Brie Larson's&nbsp;
Tess that there's hope for the family yet,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.760 --> 00:02:28.020
Letty decides to team up with Cipher for an&nbsp;
escape. What she thinks will be a quick way out,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.020 --> 00:02:31.860
though, eventually leads to the reveal that&nbsp;
she's stuck in Antarctica. We leave Letty&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.860 --> 00:02:35.265
alongside her former enemy, with no real idea&nbsp;
of what's happened to the rest of her family.

00:02:35.280 --> 00:02:38.640
Dante's attack in Rome&nbsp;
throws the family into chaos,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.640 --> 00:02:42.360
and the Toretto crew spends the rest&nbsp;
of "Fast X" divided. But at least Tej,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.360 --> 00:02:46.980
Roman, Ramsey, and Han have each other. With&nbsp;
few resources, thanks to Dante's hacking,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.980 --> 00:02:50.760
they hop around the world in search of weapons&nbsp;
they can use to head out and help Dom. They&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.760 --> 00:02:54.000
finally get a planeload of support that will&nbsp;
drop them right into the fight in Portugal.

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:57.420
What they didn't count on was&nbsp;
a last-minute betrayal. Aimes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.420 --> 00:03:00.600
who had been the acting director of The&nbsp;
Agency and was supposedly helping Dom,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.600 --> 00:03:05.160
reveals himself as Dante's longtime ally just in&nbsp;
time to hop up with a missile launcher and shoot&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.160 --> 00:03:09.660
down the plane. The last we see of Tej, Roman,&nbsp;
Ramsey, and Han, they're running for cover in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.660 --> 00:03:13.920
the back of the plane. The plane crashes around&nbsp;
the side of a mountain and bursts into flames.

00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:17.520
The back of that plane was loaded with all&nbsp;
kinds of cool tech they could use to escape,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.520 --> 00:03:19.740
and if Han's very existence&nbsp;
has taught us anything,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.740 --> 00:03:24.160
it's that Toretto crew members are pretty hard&nbsp;
to kill. So odds are we'll see them all again.

00:03:24.180 --> 00:03:28.680
It's not clear how Aimes managed to get to&nbsp;
such a significant post within The Agency,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.680 --> 00:03:33.480
but Mr. Nobody is in hiding, and Little Nobody is&nbsp;
seriously injured in the Rome incident, so he's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.480 --> 00:03:37.440
the man left in charge. Tess tries to fight him&nbsp;
on it, but Aimes' standing with the organization&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.440 --> 00:03:42.000
is such that she can't usurp his authority or stop&nbsp;
his initial efforts to take down the Toretto crew.

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:46.200
Aimes later endears himself to Dom, then&nbsp;
even later doubles back and betrays him.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:49.440
It turns out that Aimes has been working&nbsp;
alongside Dante for a full decade,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.440 --> 00:03:53.580
ever since the heist in "Fast Five," and&nbsp;
his presence in The Agency was the leg up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.580 --> 00:03:57.524
that Dante needed to achieve his goals. He&nbsp;
may have compromised the whole organization.

00:03:57.540 --> 00:04:02.220
Dante Reyes spends a lot of time talking about&nbsp;
suffering, and that his father was killed 10&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.220 --> 00:04:06.360
years earlier. By the end of the movie, he seems&nbsp;
to have achieved his goal of squeezing out every&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.360 --> 00:04:09.420
ounce of suffering from Dom that&nbsp;
he possibly can. Every member of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.420 --> 00:04:13.140
the Toretto crew is either apparently&nbsp;
dead, missing, or in dire mortal peril.

00:04:13.234 --> 00:04:19.054
"I am the man who's going to break&nbsp;
your family, piece by piece."

00:04:19.054 --> 00:04:22.740
So, does that mean Dante won? We know the&nbsp;
long answer to that question is some version&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.740 --> 00:04:26.700
of "No," because there's still at least one more&nbsp;
movie to go after this one. But for the moment,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.700 --> 00:04:29.940
there's definitely an air of victory here,&nbsp;
if only because it's going to take what's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:29.940 --> 00:04:33.480
left of the Toretto crew time to pick up&nbsp;
the pieces. The big question, then, is:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:33.480 --> 00:04:36.706
Will Dante let all this winning go&nbsp;
to his head and make a big mistake?

00:04:36.720 --> 00:04:41.220
Jason Statham's Deckard Shaw is only in&nbsp;
"Fast X" briefly, when Han decides to go&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:41.220 --> 00:04:44.760
to him for help in securing resources to&nbsp;
keep up the fight against Dante. But his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.760 --> 00:04:48.180
quick appearance is quite significant. For&nbsp;
one, it's the first time the pair have met&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:48.180 --> 00:04:52.980
since Shaw seemingly killed Han years ago. It also&nbsp;
reveals something even bigger about Dante's fight.

00:04:54.240 --> 00:04:55.680
"Let's dig some graves."

00:04:55.680 --> 00:04:59.580
While in Shaw's hideout, Ramsey discovers that&nbsp;
the money Dante stole from the crew's accounts&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:59.580 --> 00:05:03.180
has been used to hire mercenaries from around&nbsp;
the world and send them after everyone who's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.180 --> 00:05:07.320
ever helped the Toretto crew do anything.&nbsp;
That means dozens of people are now targets,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:07.320 --> 00:05:11.280
including Shaw's own mother, Queenie, who tried&nbsp;
to help Dom get out of Rome earlier in the film.

00:05:11.280 --> 00:05:15.000
With his mother in the crosshairs, Shaw&nbsp;
springs into action, loads up his gear,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:19.140
and heads out in hopes of keeping Queenie safe.&nbsp;
He's not part of the main fight against Dante, but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:19.140 --> 00:05:23.640
he is heading into something dramatic and probably&nbsp;
very bloody, leaving us to wonder how that fight&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:23.640 --> 00:05:27.540
goes. We'll just have to see what the next&nbsp;
film will reveal about Shaw's personal mission.

00:05:28.080 --> 00:05:32.820
Several new faces emerge throughout "Fast X,"&nbsp;
including Tess, Mr. Nobody's daughter who believes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:32.820 --> 00:05:37.380
in Dom no matter what the rest of the Agency&nbsp;
says. There's also Daniela Melchior's Isabel,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:37.380 --> 00:05:42.120
a Brazilian street racer who also happens to have&nbsp;
ties to Dom's past. She's the sister of Elena,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:42.120 --> 00:05:45.420
Dom's former lover and Little Brian's&nbsp;
mother, who died in "Fate of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:45.420 --> 00:05:49.500
Furious." Isabel's ties to the Toretto&nbsp;
family push her to help Dom fight Dante,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:49.500 --> 00:05:53.460
and Dom's instinct to protect his family&nbsp;
pushes him to protect Isabel at all costs.

00:05:53.460 --> 00:05:57.480
By the end of Dom's adventures in Rio,&nbsp;
Tess is seriously wounded and Isabel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:57.480 --> 00:06:01.200
is very nearly killed by Dante. Dom makes&nbsp;
the decision to put the two women together,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:01.200 --> 00:06:05.580
asking Isabel to drive Tess to a hospital,&nbsp;
leaving them both seemingly safe from Dante's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:05.580 --> 00:06:09.960
influence for now. So far, they're relatively&nbsp;
minor allies, but thanks to the mercenaries&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:09.960 --> 00:06:13.187
looking for everyone aligned with Toretto,&nbsp;
they're now in the crosshairs once again.

00:06:13.200 --> 00:06:17.880
Mia Toretto, played by Jordana Brewster,&nbsp;
has been in and out of her family's battles&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:17.880 --> 00:06:21.180
in recent years, spending a lot of time&nbsp;
off in hiding with her husband Brian and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:21.180 --> 00:06:25.920
their children. In "Fast X," she hangs around to&nbsp;
visit with her Abuelita, played by Rita Moreno,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:25.920 --> 00:06:29.820
in Los Angeles. She then watches Little&nbsp;
Brian while Dom and Letty head to Rome.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:29.820 --> 00:06:33.720
When The Agency comes for them both, Mia&nbsp;
works to fight them off alongside Jakob,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:33.720 --> 00:06:36.240
who takes Brian and tells Mia&nbsp;
to head back to her own family.

00:06:36.240 --> 00:06:39.960
By the end of the film, as far as we know,&nbsp;
Mia is safe with her husband and children,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:39.960 --> 00:06:44.220
back in hiding while the fight goes on without&nbsp;
her. But we also know that Dante has sent hired&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:44.220 --> 00:06:47.460
killers after the entire family, and&nbsp;
while Mia is good at staying hidden,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:47.460 --> 00:06:51.000
she might not be able to stay hidden forever.&nbsp;
Once she hears about what's happening with Dom,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:51.000 --> 00:06:53.700
though, she might not want to stay&nbsp;
hidden, so don't be surprised if&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:53.700 --> 00:06:56.628
she pops up again in the next movie,&nbsp;
ready to fight alongside her brother.

00:06:56.640 --> 00:07:01.620
For years, Mr. Nobody was a crucial ally to&nbsp;
the Toretto family, a leader with seemingly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:01.620 --> 00:07:05.160
infinite resources who saw enough potential&nbsp;
in Dom and his crew to shield them from the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:05.160 --> 00:07:09.660
fallout of their missions. His protege, Little&nbsp;
Nobody, picked up that baton after Mr. Nobody's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:09.660 --> 00:07:13.380
injury and remained a major supporter of the&nbsp;
family while Mr. Nobody went into hiding.

00:07:13.380 --> 00:07:18.180
Now, thanks to Dante's machinations, both Nobodies&nbsp;
are out of commission. Mr. Nobody is gone,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:18.180 --> 00:07:22.560
Little Nobody is injured, and The Agency is in&nbsp;
the hands of a turncoat. So Dom and his family&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:22.560 --> 00:07:25.980
have lost some critical support at the&nbsp;
time when they need it most. That said,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:25.980 --> 00:07:29.100
neither of the Nobodies is dead, and&nbsp;
they got to leadership positions in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:29.100 --> 00:07:33.000
an international spy agency because they're&nbsp;
smart, strategic, and know people. It wouldn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:33.000 --> 00:07:36.600
be surprising at all to see one or both of&nbsp;
them come roaring back in the next film.

00:07:37.140 --> 00:07:41.040
Cipher begins "Fast X" in a pretty&nbsp;
low place. Dante tracked her down,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:41.040 --> 00:07:44.100
blackmailed all of her men, and&nbsp;
used her own resources against her,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:44.100 --> 00:07:48.240
leaving her nearly dead and in the hands of The&nbsp;
Agency. But while Cipher's been down before,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:48.240 --> 00:07:51.600
she's never been down for long, and she&nbsp;
reveals that she has an escape plan.

00:07:51.900 --> 00:07:54.420
"She's a monster to battle with, I gotta say."

00:07:54.420 --> 00:07:58.920
At the Agency black site in Antarctica, Cipher&nbsp;
reveals that she's not out of options after all,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:58.920 --> 00:08:02.340
and summons a submarine like the one she&nbsp;
commanded in "Fate of the Furious" up out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:02.340 --> 00:08:06.540
of the ice. That's impressive enough, but&nbsp;
the real jaw-dropping reveal is that she's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:06.540 --> 00:08:11.100
working with none other than Gal Gadot's Gisele&nbsp;
Yashar, who seemingly died in "Fast &amp; Furious&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:11.100 --> 00:08:15.180
6." Gisele's presence after years away&nbsp;
raises a whole new round of questions,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:15.180 --> 00:08:19.980
including how Han might react when he sees her&nbsp;
again. Cipher is clearly still full of surprises,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:19.980 --> 00:08:22.607
and those surprises might just&nbsp;
force Dom to team up with her.

00:08:22.620 --> 00:08:26.460
Dante's war will clearly keep going&nbsp;
into the next film. It's a big story,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:26.460 --> 00:08:28.200
so it keeps going after the credits roll.

00:08:28.200 --> 00:08:31.560
In the film's mid-credits sequence,&nbsp;
Dante targets another former Toretto&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:31.560 --> 00:08:35.700
ally who played a major role in the death of his&nbsp;
father: Luke Hobbs, played by Dwayne Johnson,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:35.700 --> 00:08:40.080
who delivered the fatal shot to Hernan&nbsp;
Reyes in "Fast Five." Hobbs discovers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:40.080 --> 00:08:43.560
that Dante has tracked him down, and hears a&nbsp;
message that "the devil" is coming for him.

00:08:43.560 --> 00:08:47.880
Naturally, Hobbs doesn't back down from the&nbsp;
fight. The question now is how his fight with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:47.880 --> 00:08:52.080
Dante will connect to Dom's, and vice versa. The&nbsp;
last time we saw them together within the films,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:52.080 --> 00:08:55.320
they were allies who'd just finished a&nbsp;
mission that reunited the family. But&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:55.320 --> 00:08:59.021
Hobbs has been off on his own for a while, so&nbsp;
it's hard to tell just how close they'll get.

00:08:59.040 --> 00:09:03.420
Dom and Mia's grandmother is only present&nbsp;
in "Fast X" for a few minutes early on,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:03.420 --> 00:09:07.920
but she leaves a lasting impression. Like Dom,&nbsp;
his grandmother has endured tremendous loss,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:07.920 --> 00:09:12.000
and she's learned through that loss to value and&nbsp;
protect the family that she has left. For Dom,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:12.000 --> 00:09:16.320
the fight is much closer, much more tangible,&nbsp;
even when all he's doing is teaching Little B&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:16.320 --> 00:09:19.380
to drive. So when his grandmother tells&nbsp;
him that with his family by his side,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:19.380 --> 00:09:21.240
he can do anything, that really means something.

00:09:21.240 --> 00:09:25.140
Dom clings to the idea that if he sticks&nbsp;
with the ones he loves and has faith,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:25.140 --> 00:09:28.740
they can survive what's coming for them,&nbsp;
no matter how bad it gets. We don't get to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:28.740 --> 00:09:32.220
see how he deals with the latest round of&nbsp;
losses right away, since the film ends on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:32.220 --> 00:09:38.333
a cliffhanger. But we do know where Dom's focus&nbsp;
is and what he values, because Abuelita told us.

